Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

All,

Attached is a tool we are developing to aid understanding of our portfolio =
of products as they "map" into the sewer market, and relative financial opp=
ortunity.

This map also speaks to strategy, and tactics.  These we will breakdown and=
 detail later.

There are four levels.
Level 1:  The Sewer Market Space.
Level 2:  The three sewer application types; Gravity Sewer, Pressure Sewer,=
 Vacuum Sewer.  The Pressure Sewer application has two subtypes; Force Main=
 and Grinder Systems.
Level 3:  The pipe types that may be used in the application.
Level 4:  Harco fitting/product options that might be used according to pip=
e type in an application.

Within a pipe type the fitting products are substitutes for one another.  E=
ach pipe type is a potential substitute for every other pipe type within an=
 application.

The font sizes of the Harco fitting products on the map are a measure of th=
eir relative unit profit and margin potential as well as Harco's advantage =
by way of differentiation versus competing products for a given pipe type w=
ithin an application.  The font sizes of the pipe types speak to their rela=
tive profit potential for Harco within a given application.

These relative advantages are a matter of debate and can vary.

The Sales Team's role is to cause customer appreciation for Harco products =
that translates into demand that results in profitable sales.  The informat=
ion in the map will help inform the Sales Team's priorities and efforts to =
that end.

More later.

J

